.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
plugin that creates and handles a 'rubberband' selection 

this selection by default looks like that in the nautilus file-manager.
.PP
the factory installs a variety of properties; see below. these properties can be set in themes, or from the typebuffer, e.g. 'rubberboxbordercolour ff00ff
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "static int rb_num_listener (noir_prop_bag * b, noir_prop * e, int tag, void * data)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
listen for changes in our numeric properties. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
NOIR_SUCC, or an error-code. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIb\fP - the bag 
.br
\fIe\fP - the property 
.br
\fItag\fP - our index/tag for the property that has changed 
.br
\fIdata\fP - our parameter-struct for this plugin, for faster access to the properties' values
.RE
.PP

